spec:
  grid: 20x20, black background
  objects: 3-5 distinct foreground colors; each color is one object
  statics: 1-3 solid filled rectangles, 3-8 rows x 5-9 cols [observed]
  sliders: 2-3 objects, each a solid rectangular body (3-7 rows x 3-9 cols, min dim >= 3) plus a 1-pixel-wide tail
  tail:
    length: 2-6 cells
    direction: any cardinal (R/L/U/D)
    attachment: extends from an interior row/col of the body (never an edge row/col)
  z-order: statics drawn first as full rectangles; slider (body+tail) drawn on top, occluding statics
  occlusion: slider bodies may partially overlap static bboxes in input; statics never overlap each other
  slider constraints:
    body is fully visible (no other color within body region)
    slider bboxes (body+tail) do not overlap each other
    translated body (body shifted by tail_len in tail_dir) stays within grid bounds
    translated bodies do not overlap each other
  output:
    statics restored as full rectangles (un-occluded)
    slider tails erased; bodies translated by tail_length in tail_direction
    translated slider bodies drawn on top of restored statics

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick 3-5 distinct non-black colors; assign 2-3 as sliders, rest as statics
    2. For each slider, choose body dims (3-7 x 3-9, min dim >= 3), a cardinal direction, and tail length 2-6
    3. For each static, choose dims (3-8 x 5-9)
